WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.505 --> 00:00:18.476
The next evening, after we tied up the raft, I went into a nearby town with the king

2
00:00:18.596 --> 00:00:19.077
and the duke.

3
00:00:19.998 --> 00:00:26.623
Nearly everyone was at an outdoor religious meeting, and the king immediately thought of a way to make

4
00:00:26.703 --> 00:00:27.224
money from it.

5
00:00:28.476 --> 00:00:32.819
The king and I stood at the back of the crowd and listened for a while as the

6
00:00:32.859 --> 00:00:34.580
townspeople sang some hymns.

7
00:00:35.481 --> 00:00:40.924
Then the preacher said that anyone who had sinned should come forward and promise to live a better

8
00:00:40.964 --> 00:00:45.968
life. The king leaped up and ran to the front of the meeting.

9
00:00:46.888 --> 00:00:51.011
He said that he had been a pirate in the Indian Ocean for thirty years.

10
00:00:52.312 --> 00:00:55.294
Now he understood that this was a bad way to live.

11
00:00:55.314 --> 00:01:03.381
"All I want now," he said, "is to go back to the ocean and tell all the other

12
00:01:03.481 --> 00:01:07.442
pirates to stop their evil ways and live a good life."

13
00:01:12.084 --> 00:01:13.984
Then he began to cry with shame.

14
00:01:15.045 --> 00:01:18.385
Many people in the crowd believed him and began to cry too.

15
00:01:18.405 --> 00:01:22.547
"Let's collect some money for him to help him do his good work!"

16
00:01:22.827 --> 00:01:24.127
yelled someone in the crowd.

17
00:01:24.847 --> 00:01:29.501
The townspeople passed a hat around to collect money and gave all of it to the king.

18
00:01:30.302 --> 00:01:31.862
He hugged them and thanked them.

19
00:01:32.763 --> 00:01:38.627
When we got back to the raft, we found that he had collected 87 dollars and 75 cents.

20
00:01:40.027 --> 00:01:42.349
The duke had been busy in town too.

21
00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:46.591
He had thought of a clever way that we could travel in the daytime.

22
00:01:47.512 --> 00:01:49.373
He showed us a poster he had printed.

23
00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:57.915
It said "Two-Hundred Dollar Reward" in big letters; underneath, it described a black slave who had escaped from

24
00:01:57.975 --> 00:01:59.576
a plantation near New Orleans.

25
00:02:01.637 --> 00:02:06.400
If other boats on the river came too close to our raft, we could tie Jim up so

26
00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:08.202
it would look as if he was our prisoner.

27
00:02:09.142 --> 00:02:14.246
Then we could show people the poster and tell them we were taking Jim south to New Orleans

28
00:02:14.306 --> 00:02:15.246
to get the reward.

29
00:02:16.527 --> 00:02:22.011
For the next two days, as we continued south on the river, the king and the duke rehearsed

30
00:02:22.031 --> 00:02:23.152
their play on the raft.

31
00:02:24.168 --> 00:02:29.271
The duke had two wooden swords in his suitcase, and the two men practiced a fight scene.

32
00:02:30.271 --> 00:02:34.293
On the third day, we arrived at a place in Arkansas called Bricksville.

33
00:02:36.054 --> 00:02:41.357
A circus would be putting on a show in the afternoon, and the town was crowded with people

34
00:02:41.677 --> 00:02:43.738
who had come from the countryside to see it.

35
00:02:44.698 --> 00:02:48.080
The duke rented a hall where the play could be staged that evening.

36
00:02:49.628 --> 00:02:55.312
He also got some posters printed, announcing the play, and walked around town handing them out.

37
00:02:56.032 --> 00:03:00.776
The charge would be 25 cents for each adult and 10 cents for each child.

38
00:03:01.696 --> 00:03:05.799
In the afternoon, I snuck under the edge of the tent to watch the circus.

39
00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:13.164
I saw handsome men, and women who looked like queens, with glittering jewels all over their costumes.

40
00:03:14.225 --> 00:03:18.728
They stood up on the backs of horses that galloped around and around the circus ring.

41
00:03:19.496 --> 00:03:22.078
It was the most amazing sight I had ever seen.

42
00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:31.024
That night, the king and duke put on their Shakespearean play, but only 12 people came.

43
00:03:32.065 --> 00:03:35.727
They laughed through the whole play, which wasn't supposed to be funny.

44
00:03:36.708 --> 00:03:42.091
Afterward, the duke said that the people of Arkansas were too stupid to appreciate Shakespeare.

45
00:03:42.111 --> 00:03:44.913
"Tomorrow night," he said.

46
00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:50.136
"We'll give them the show they deserve—the Royal Nonesuch."

47
00:03:50.156 --> 00:03:54.901
The duke got new posters printed with the name of the show and the new price: fifty cents.

48
00:03:56.062 --> 00:03:59.465
At the bottom, the poster said, "No women and children admitted."

49
00:04:00.866 --> 00:04:03.408
That evening, the theater was packed with men.

50
00:04:04.629 --> 00:04:10.354
The duke stood in front of the crowd and announced, "You are about to see the most thrilling

51
00:04:10.414 --> 00:04:12.696
performance in the history of theater!"

52
00:04:13.937 --> 00:04:16.519
Then the king hurried onto the stage on all fours.

53
00:04:17.344 --> 00:04:22.008
He wore no clothes, and his skin was painted all over with stripes of different colors.

54
00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:26.252
The crowd roared with laughter and clapped.

55
00:04:27.293 --> 00:04:30.436
The king hopped off the stage and the duke reappeared.

56
00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:35.581
If they had enjoyed the show, he said, they should tell their friends to come the next night.

57
00:04:36.682 --> 00:04:40.905
People in the audience shouted angrily, "Is the show over already?

58
00:04:41.286 --> 00:04:43.328
You charged us fifty cents for this?"

59
00:04:44.704 --> 00:04:51.128
Then a tall man in the audience stood up and said, "Yes, we've been tricked, gentlemen, but we

60
00:04:51.168 --> 00:04:53.009
don't want the whole town laughing at us.

61
00:04:53.949 --> 00:04:57.391
Let's leave here and tell all the other men in town to see the show.

62
00:04:58.392 --> 00:05:01.453
Then we'll all be fools, and no one will be laughing at anyone else."

63
00:05:02.874 --> 00:05:07.797
Everyone must have followed his advice because our theater was filled again the next night.

64
00:05:08.737 --> 00:05:11.779
Once again, the king hopped around for a couple of minutes.

65
00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:17.944
But on the third night, the people arriving at the theater were angry men who had already seen

66
00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:18.384
the show.

67
00:05:19.705 --> 00:05:24.890
I watched them as they came inside and I saw that they were bringing rotten eggs and cabbages

68
00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:26.011
to throw at the stage.

69
00:05:27.072 --> 00:05:31.596
I ran backstage and told the king and duke that they should get out of town at once.

70
00:05:32.497 --> 00:05:35.179
We all ran back to the raft where Jim was waiting.

71
00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:40.404
By the time the audience realized we were gone, we had started down the river.

72
00:05:41.492 --> 00:05:44.574
We didn't light our lantern until we were ten kilometers south.

73
00:05:45.774 --> 00:05:49.797
Then we had our supper on the raft, while the king and duke counted their earnings.

74
00:05:50.677 --> 00:05:52.738
They had 465 dollars.

75
00:05:53.379 --> 00:05:55.320
I had never seen so much money.
